{
 "id": "ep012",
 "title": "Why Are 3 Million Seniors Losing Their Health Plans?",
 "voice": "am_michael",
 "speed": 1.0,
 "description": "Nearly 3.2 million Americans in Medicare Advantage must pick a new plan for 2027 because their plan is being discontinued, including about 1 million from Humana (about 600,000) and UnitedHealthcare (about 390,000), as CBS News reported on October 23, 2026. We go through what Medicare Advantage is, why insurers say they are cutting (higher costs, more use of care, lower federal payments), why critics say the program is still overpaid (MedPAC: about 14% more than traditional Medicare), what the Medicare agency (CMS) says, who is hit hardest (rural counties, people with high costs, prescriptions), and the key dates: open enrollment Oct 15 - Dec 7, a special window to the end of February if your plan ends, and the Medigap guaranteed-issue window.\n\nGeneral information only, not medical, legal or financial advice. Check medicare.gov or your state's free SHIP counselling program for your own situation. Ruth, Dave and Linda are made-up characters. Real people are shown as generic labelled stick figures; quotes are attributed as reported.\n\nSources:\nCBS News, Humana, UnitedHealthcare ending Medicare Advantage plans for 1 million seniors (Oct 23, 2026): https://www.cbsnews.com/news/humana-unitedhealthcare-end-medicare-advantage-plans/\nHealthcare Dive, Here's how much insurers are cutting Medicare Advantage plans for 2027: https://www.healthcaredive.com/news/medicare-advantage-cuts-2027-cms-landscape/831563/\nMarketplace, As Medicare open enrollment begins, millions of seniors will have to pick a new plan (Oct 14, 2026): https://www.marketplace.org/story/2026/10/14/why-some-insurers-are-dropping-medicare-advantage-plans\n24/7 Wall St., 3.2 million seniors will lose their Medicare Advantage plans in 2027 (Oct 19, 2026; citing CNN, KFF, Medicare Market Insights): https://247wallst.com/health-and-healthcare/2026/10/19/3-2-million-seniors-will-lose-their-medicare-advantage-plans-in-2027-and-their-replacement-options-are-shrinking/\nStraight Arrow News, Medicare open enrollment begins as millions face fewer plans, higher costs: https://san.com/cc/medicare-open-enrollment-begins-as-millions-face-fewer-plans-higher-costs/\nKFF, Medicare Advantage in 2026: Enrollment Update and Key Trends: https://www.kff.org/medicare/fact-sheet/medicare-advantage/\nMedPAC, March 2026 report press release: https://www.medpac.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/March_2026_MedPAC_Report_Press_Release_SEC.pdf\nMoney Talks News, Your Medicare Advantage plan won't be back in 2027? The Medigap window: https://www.moneytalksnews.com/your-medicare-advantage-plan-wont-be-back-in-a-cpa-on-the-medigap-window-that-protects-you/\n\n#medicare #medicareadvantage #openenrollment #explained #stickfigure #news",
